{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-08T21:05:09.210Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both the task `verify` and the proposal's `pnpm verify` pass, and the result file is written.\n\nSummary of what I did:\n\n- **`src/core/spec/assumptions.ts`** (new): exports `readAssumptions(body)` returning `readonly string[] | null`. It locates `## Assumptions` exactly as `readSurfaceSection` locates `## Surface`, strips HTML comments, trims and drops empty lines, strips a leading `- ` marker, returns `null` for an absent section, `[]` when the only line is `None`, and the assumption lines otherwise. Also exports `assumptionsSectionIsEmpty(body)` and `PROPOSAL_ASSUMPTIONS_ERROR`.\n- **`src/core/spec/linter.ts`**: added the import and a single check in `lintChangeFolder` right after the Surface check, under the same `resolvedDoc.kind === 'proposal'` exemption, recording the assumptions error on the proposal file with `section: 'Assumptions'`. A missing section gives no finding, keeping all existing proposals silent.\n- **`tests/assumptions-lint.test.ts`** (new): a table over `readAssumptions` plus `lintChangeFolder` cases on a scaffolded temp project for the comment-only failure, the missing-section exemption, and the `None`/list acceptances.\n\nOne deviation noted in the result: the empty-section error can't be derived from `readAssumptions` alone (comment-only and `None` both yield `[]`), so I added the small `assumptionsSectionIsEmpty` helper in the same file to keep the `linter.ts` call short, as the task asked."}}
